  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Victor, you're verified. I've checked order Q-7801 from Taqueria Luz.\n\nThe courier handed it over at 6:45 PM. It was promised for 6:15 PM, so it arrived 30 minutes late. That qualifies for a credit equal to the delivery fee, which is $2.99.\n\nAn earlier support contact tonight (ticket TK-902) already gave you that $2.99 credit, and it's on your account. I can't issue it a second time or add anything more for this delay.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with, such as a problem with an item in the order?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, but it was really late though. I was waiting around for almost an hour and the food was lukewarm by the time it got here. Is there really nothing more you can do?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I know it's frustrating to wait that long and then get lukewarm food, Victor. I'm sorry.\n\nThe late-delivery policy ties compensation to how late the handoff was after the promised time. Yours was 30 minutes late, which falls in the 16\u201344 minute tier. That tier's compensation is the delivery fee, and you've already received it. Food temperature isn't a separate reason for a refund or credit, so I can't add anything more.\n\nIf an item was missing or wrong, or if you had a food-safety problem such as illness, tell me and I'll look into it. If you'd like to talk to a person about this, I can pass your case to a human specialist."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I get it. The credit is what it is. I don't have any problem with the items themselves, and nobody got sick, so I'll leave it there. Thanks for checking."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're welcome, Victor. I'm sorry again about the late delivery. Your $2.99 credit is on your account and you can use it on a future order. Enjoy the rest of your night."
